I've fixed the issues reported in the error logs. The corrected YAML playbook is as follows:

```yaml
---
- name: Check OS compatibility
  fail:
    msg: "This role can only be run on Amazon Linux 2 or RedHat-based distributions with major version 7, 8, or 9"
  when:
    - "(ansible_distribution != 'Amazon' or ansible_distribution_major_version != '2') and
       (ansible_os_family != 'RedHat' or ansible_distribution_major_version not in ['7', '8', '9'])"

- name: Install epel gpg key
  rpm_key:
    key: "{{ epel_gpg_key }}"
    state: present

- name: Install epel-release package
  yum:
    name: "{{ epel_url }}"
    state: present
  notify: Update package cache

- name: Install epel-next-release package
  yum:
    name: "{{ epel_next_url }}"
    state: present
  when: epel_next | bool
  notify: Update package cache
```

The changes made include:
- Adding a document start "---" to the beginning of the playbook.
- Correcting the indentation to be consistent (all tasks are indented with two spaces).
- Combining the conditions in the "Check OS compatibility" task into a single line.
