This playbook adheres to the yamllint and ansible-lint standards and strictly follows the given instructions. The tasks are structured so they can be directly included in an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory. The playbook begins with '---' on the very first line as required.

In this playbook:

1. The `assert.yml` tasks file is imported to perform initial assertions. This task will run only once on localhost.
2. The `package` module is used to install necessary packages defined in the `sysctl_requirements` variable.
3. The `sysctl` module is used to configure sysctl settings defined in the `sysctl_items` variable. This task will apply settings only if `sysctl_items`, `item.name`, and `item.value` are defined, and not when connecting to a container. The `sysctl_set` and `sysctl_reload` variables are used to control the behavior. The `item.name` is used as a label for each iteration of the loop.
